WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.350
Now, when it comes to optimizing your

00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:03.790
claw.md, it is actually useful to note

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:06.990
that there are two claw.mds in your

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.230
device. And so, if you go to Cloud Code

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:10.870
and actually just ask it to give you the

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:13.350
path of your root claw.md and your

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:15.670
project claw.md, you'll actually be able

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:18.270
to see what exactly those different

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:20.550
employee handbooks contain. And so, for

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:22.230
me, you can see that there is two

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:24.270
different claw.mds that we have here.

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:25.790
The one we were viewing in previous

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:28.750
modules is this claw.md that exists for

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:30.790
this project. Meaning the folder that

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.190
you open in VS Code where Cloud Code is

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:35.110
operating within, that includes all of

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:36.510
the operating instructions that we just

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:38.070
discussed. And so, if we go to that

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:40.150
claw.md, there you can find all of the

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:42.510
rules, the goals, the identity, as well

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:44.990
as the map of our workspace. Now, it is

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:46.590
sometimes useful to know that there is

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:48.990
actually another claw.md that applies

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:51.230
for all of your projects globally. And

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:53.870
it is usually contained in your users

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:55.750
folder here. But for me, you can see

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:58.110
that there is no detail on the claw.md

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:00.110
here because what I'm finding for most

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:02.110
power users, including myself, operating

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:04.229
within one project and having your sort

00:01:04.239 --> 00:01:06.310
of second brain on operating system in

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:08.670
just one folder is more effective versus

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:10.670
having different projects with their own

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:13.350
claw.mds. And so, because there is only

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:15.110
one project and workspace anyway that

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:16.590
you need to manage, then usually there

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:19.470
is no requirement for you to even have a

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:22.070
global claw.md. But that is just useful

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:23.710
to know for you to complete the picture

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:25.990
of how Cloud Code works at the moment.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:28.550
And very simply put, those two claw.mds,

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:30.230
one applies to the whole house, so they

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:31.950
are global rules, while the one that I

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:34.070
recommend for you to focus on would be

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:37.040
the project rules.
